      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Bike Transport from Bangalore</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Transporting a vehicle from Bangalore to Hubli requires meticulous preparation of legal and logistical documentation to ensure a seamless, compliant, and secure journey. While the route is a straightforward highway drive, the absence of proper paperwork can lead to significant delays, fines, or even confiscation by transport authorities.</p>
<p>To mitigate these risks, shippers must compile a specific set of essential documents before handing over the keys to the logistics provider. This guide details the mandatory paperwork and highlights the critical importance of comprehensive insurance coverage for your vehicle.</p>

<p>The foundational requirement for any interstate vehicle movement is the <strong>self-attested photocopy of the Registration Certificate (RC)</strong>. This document serves as the primary proof of ownership.</p>
<p>It is crucial that the name on the RC matches the name of the person authorizing the transport. While the original RC is typically not required to be handed over to the carrier, a high-quality, self-attested copy must accompany the vehicle or be verified by the logistics team to establish legal authority for the transit.</p>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">In addition to ownership proof, you must provide a copy of the <strong>current Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate</strong>.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Although the vehicle is being transported on a carrier and not driven on public roads, transport agencies and state transport authorities often require a valid PUC to verify that the vehicle is legally fit for registration and transit.</span></li></ul>
<p>Ensuring this certificate is current prevents any bureaucratic hurdles at checkposts or during final delivery in Hubli.</p>

<p>The third critical document is the <strong>valid insurance certificate</strong>. While your personal comprehensive insurance policy may cover the vehicle, it is not sufficient for the specific risks involved in third-party transport. Therefore, you must also secure an <strong>IBA-approved consignment bilty</strong>.</p>
<p>This document acts as the contract between you and the logistics provider, detailing the vehicle’s condition, the transit route, and the agreed-upon liability terms. The bilty is the primary legal instrument used for any claims or disputes that may arise during the move.</p>

