<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #0b132b; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 15px;">
    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transport From Bangalore To Hubli</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><h3>Destination Delivery Handover Process for Two‑Wheeler & Motorcycle</h3>

<div style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.08); border-left: 4px solid #f59e0b; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 18px 22px; margin: 24px 0;"><h4 style="color: #f59e0b; font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle" style="margin-right: 8px;"></i>Important Logistics Advisory</h4><div style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.92rem; margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">When a two‑wheeler or motorcycle reaches its final destination, a structured handover ensures that the vehicle is transferred in the exact condition documented at pickup. The procedure combines visual verification, mileage confirmation, and a formal sign‑off, creating a transparent record for both the logistics provider and the recipient.</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Daylight Condition Re‑inspection</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>Conduct the inspection under natural daylight to eliminate shadows or artificial lighting that could mask surface defects.</li>
        <li>Compare the vehicle’s current appearance with the original pickup photographs, checking for scratches, dents, paint chips, or any missing accessories.</li>
        <li>Note any discrepancies on the handover checklist and photograph the issue for immediate documentation.</li>
    </ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Odometer Verification Against LR Bilty</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>Read the odometer directly from the instrument cluster and record the figure on the handover form.</li>
        <li>Cross‑check this reading with the mileage recorded on the LR (Lorry Receipt) bilty that accompanied the shipment.</li>
        <li>If a variance greater than 5 km is observed, investigate possible causes (e.g., route deviation, tampering) before proceeding.</li>
    </ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Signed Condition Sign‑off</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>The recipient reviews the inspection checklist, photographs, and odometer comparison.</li>
        <li>Both parties sign the condition report, confirming that the vehicle has been received in the documented state.</li>
        <li>A copy of the signed report is retained by the logistics team, and the recipient receives the original for their records.</li>
    </ul>
</li>
</ul>

<p>This three‑step handover creates a reliable audit trail. The daylight re‑inspection eliminates disputes over visual damage, the odometer check safeguards against mileage fraud, and the signed sign‑off provides legal acknowledgment of the vehicle’s condition at delivery.</div></div>

<p>Key stakeholders involved are:</p>

<ul>
<li>Delivery personnel who perform the on‑site inspection and collect signatures.</li>
<li>The recipient or authorized representative who validates the condition and mileage.</li>
<li>The logistics coordination team that prepares the LR bilty, maintains photographic records, and archives the signed handover documents.</li>
</ul>

<p>By adhering to this protocol, companies ensure a smooth, accountable transfer that protects both the sender’s assets and the recipient’s expectations.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



